#!/bin/sh
# flashes the image file $2 with ofgwrite and its options $3, unpacked
# into $1/.ofgwrite. ofgwrite does not come back when it flashes the slot
# running: it stops Neutrino, writes from RAM and restarts the box

DIR="$1/.ofgwrite"
rm -rf "$DIR"
mkdir -p "$DIR" || exit 1
case "$2" in
	*.zip) unzip -o -q "$2" -d "$DIR" ;;
	*) tar -xzf "$2" -C "$DIR" ;;
esac
IMG=$(find "$DIR" -name rootfs.tar.bz2 | head -n 1)
if [ -z "$IMG" ]; then
	echo "no rootfs.tar.bz2 in $2"
	rm -rf "$DIR"
	exit 1
fi

for i in $(cat /proc/cmdline); do
	case "$i" in rootsubdir=*) SUB=${i#rootsubdir=} ;; esac
done
ofgwrite $3 "$(dirname "$IMG")"
RET=$?
[ "${3#-m}" = "$(echo "$SUB" | sed 's/.*[^0-9]//')" ] || rm -rf "$DIR"
exit $RET
